frontends/dri: list LINEAR for YUV formats when the driver has no modifier query.

radeonsi before GFX9 (Polaris and older) has no query_dmabuf_modifiers,
so eglQueryDmaBufModifiersEXT returns no modifiers for any format
("implicit only"). Importing a YUV dma-buf with an explicit LINEAR
modifier works on such a driver (format_and_modifier_supported accepts it
without is_dmabuf_modifier_supported), but importers that negotiate
explicit modifiers see none: GStreamer's glupload advertises no DMA_DRM
formats, so vah264dec's NV12:0x0 output (see the frontends/va patch)
cannot be imported and every frame is copied through system memory.

For YUV formats, report DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR (external-only as for
native sampling) when the screen has no modifier query. RGB formats keep
the implicit-only answer, so DRI3/glamor modifier negotiation is
unchanged. Found on a Radeon Pro 560 (Polaris 11) under OpenIndiana.
Upstreamable (not yet submitted).

--- src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c.orig
+++ src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
@@ -1324,6 +1324,22 @@
             for (int i = 0; i < *count; i++)
                external_only[i] = true;
          }
+      } else if (util_format_is_yuv(format)) {
+         /* No modifier query (radeonsi before GFX9, for one): such a
+          * driver still imports a YUV buffer with an explicit LINEAR
+          * modifier (format_and_modifier_supported), and its video
+          * buffers are linear. List LINEAR, so that importers which
+          * negotiate explicit modifiers (GStreamer's glupload against
+          * vah264dec's DMA_DRM NV12:0x0) can use the zero-copy path.
+          * RGB formats keep the implicit-only answer, so DRI3/glamor
+          * modifier negotiation is unchanged.
+          */
+         if (max > 0) {
+            modifiers[0] = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+            if (external_only)
+               external_only[0] = !native_sampling;
+         }
+         *count = 1;
       } else {
          *count = 0;
       }
